 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_22
+----------------
+| macOS version: 27.0.1 (build 26A434)
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: none known; ``gpu-kosmickrisp-raster-state`` (gs and
+  tes-gs stages, host project test)
+| Comments:
+
+The setup kernel of a geometry shader draw, ``libkk_gs_setup_indirect``,
+first checks that the draw's sizes do not overflow, with the library's
+``poly_u32_checked_mul``: ``b != 0 && a > UINT_MAX / b``. Now and then the
+compiled kernel takes the invalid branch with correct inputs, and the draw's
+geometry is lost. On an Apple7 GPU (M1 Ultra) under macOS 27.0.1, with the
+encoder of a render pass started late, about one iteration in a hundred of
+the test's gs and tes-gs stages fails. The draw count, the instance count,
+the vertex output mask and the geometry shader's output vertex count and
+stride are correct in the GPU's view on both sides of the dispatch, and a copy
+of the kernel dispatched before and after it computes valid from them, while
+the kernel itself zeroes the grids and returns. It is all or nothing per
+recording: every geometry setup of the failing command buffer is refused,
+while the same command buffer passed every one in the recording before. The
+same compiled kernel dispatched alone, millions of times, never fails, and an
+edit that does not change what the kernel computes but changes the code the
+compiler generates for the validity test makes the failure disappear. The
+validity test runs in the constant program (the preamble) of the Apple GPU
+binary, whose size differs between the variants that fail and those that do
+not.
+
+The workaround tests the overflow of the multiplications of that block with
+``mul_hi``, whose result is zero exactly when the product fits in 32 bits
+(a zero factor included), and so does without the divisions the five checks
+compile to: five checks, four distinct divisors, so four 32-bit divisions.
+Two programs were measured, in the same load windows as the intact kernel.
+A hand-patched build of the kernel with these multiplications failed in none
+of 559 iterations, against 5 of 696 for the intact kernel; its Apple binary
+is not the shipped one (its constant program is 3648 bytes, the shipped one's
+3712). The shipped kernel failed in none of 680 iterations, against 3 of 680
+for the intact kernel as the control. The mechanism inside the compiler is
+inferred, not shown, and an unrelated edit may move the defect to another
+kernel.
+
+To qualify removing the workaround, first show that the harness reproduces
+the failure in its load window: run the raster-state test's gs and tes-gs
+stages with the late encoder start on against the intact kernel (the
+multiplications as ``poly_u32_checked_mul``) on macOS 27.0.1 and an Apple7
+GPU, where 3 to 5 iterations in 700 fail. Then run the intact kernel on the OS
+and GPU under test. A remaining defect fails at least once in 600 iterations
+with about 93 percent probability at that rate, so 600 clean iterations
+qualify the removal for that combination and one failure keeps the
+workaround.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-11-12: Workaround implemented, with the figures of the shipped kernel
+  and the condition for removing it
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_19
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 27.0
